<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Betsimisaraka Confederation</h1><p class="st-meta">1712 CE – 1817 CE (approx.) · capital Fenoarivo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An east Malagasy confederation forged by Ratsimilaho, son of an English pirate, which controlled trade with the French islands.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Early 18th-century east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> was dominated by Tsikoa clans from the south and by the descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a> who had settled at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ile-sainte-marie">Ile Sainte-Marie</a> and the coast. Around 1712 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratsimilaho">Ratsimilaho</a>, son of the English pirate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-white-pirate">Thomas White</a> and a Malagasy princess, united the northern clans against the Tsikoa and was chosen king, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fenoarivo-atsinanana">Fenoarivo</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratsimilaho">Ratsimilaho</a> governed through alliances and assemblies of clan chiefs, and the mixed-descent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zana-malata">Zana-malata</a> formed an elite. The confederation supplied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and slaves to French <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ile-bourbon">Ile Bourbon</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/isle-de-france">Isle de France</a> through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toamasina">Toamasina</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/foulpointe">Foulpointe</a>. He married a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakalava">Sakalava</a> princess of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/boina">Boina</a> to secure alliances.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratsimilaho">Ratsimilaho's</a> death in 1750 the confederation fragmented among rival chiefs, and French traders gained influence. In 1817 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radama-i">Radama I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/merina-kingdom">Merina Kingdom</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toamasina">Toamasina</a>, bringing the east coast under Merina rule.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1712 CE – 1817 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.77%;width:2.09%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1712 CE – 1817 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Fenoarivo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ratsimilaho</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Malagasy religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malagasy (Betsimisaraka)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/madagascar">Madagascar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Betsimisaraka, Ratsimilaho's kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1764&amp;focus=betsimisaraka-confederation" aria-label="Betsimisaraka Confederation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5963 2879 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Betsimisaraka Confederation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6283 3135L6286 3134"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6286 3134h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6283 3135h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6283 3135h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Fenoarivo. <a href="/atlas?year=1764&amp;focus=betsimisaraka-confederation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

